---
import Tool from '../../layouts/Tool.astro';
---
<Tool title="Dimensional weight checker" description="Check whether a parcel is billed on actual or dimensional weight, using the dimensional divisor from your own carrier rate guide or contract." lede="Carriers can bill on the greater of actual weight and dimensional (volumetric) weight. Enter the divisor your carrier publishes for your service and see which applies.">
  <form slot="calc" class="calc" id="dw" onsubmit="this.dispatchEvent(new Event('input'));return false">
    <fieldset><legend>Parcel</legend>
      <div class="field"><label for="u">Units</label><select id="u"><option value="in">inches and pounds</option><option value="cm">centimeters and kilograms</option></select></div>
      <div class="field"><label for="l">Length</label><input id="l" type="number" min="0" step="0.1" value="12" inputmode="decimal" /></div>
      <div class="field"><label for="w">Width</label><input id="w" type="number" min="0" step="0.1" value="9" inputmode="decimal" /></div>
      <div class="field"><label for="h">Height</label><input id="h" type="number" min="0" step="0.1" value="4" inputmode="decimal" /></div>
      <div class="field"><label for="a">Actual weight</label><input id="a" type="number" min="0" step="0.01" value="1.5" inputmode="decimal" /></div>
      <div class="field"><label for="d">Dimensional divisor <span class="hint">Required. Copy it from your carrier’s current rate guide or your contract for the service you use. There is no single correct number.</span></label><input id="d" type="number" min="1" step="1" placeholder="e.g. from your rate guide" inputmode="numeric" /></div>
      <button class="btn btn-tag" type="submit">Calculate</button>
    </fieldset>
    <fieldset aria-live="polite"><legend>Result</legend>
      <div class="out"><span>Volume</span><span class="v" id="o-vol">—</span></div>
      <div class="out"><span>Dimensional weight</span><span class="v" id="o-dim">—</span></div>
      <div class="out"><span>Actual weight</span><span class="v" id="o-act">—</span></div>
      <div class="out big"><span>Greater of the two</span><span class="v" id="o-bill">—</span></div>
      <div class="out"><span>Rounded up to whole unit</span><span class="v" id="o-round">—</span></div>
      <p class="verdict" id="o-v">Enter your carrier’s divisor to see the result.</p>
    </fieldset>
  </form>
  <h2>How the calculation works</h2>
  <p>Dimensional weight is the parcel’s volume divided by a divisor: <code>length × width × height ÷ divisor</code>. With inches the result is in pounds; with centimeters it is in kilograms. The calculator then takes the greater of that figure and the actual weight, and also shows it rounded up to the next whole pound or kilogram, because many rate tables are priced in whole weight units.</p>
  <h2>Why the divisor is left blank</h2>
  <p>Divisors differ by carrier, by service (ground, air, international), and by contract, and carriers change them. A default value would be a fact this site could not keep current for every reader, so the field is empty until you enter the figure printed in your own rate guide or agreement. Measure the packed parcel at its longest points, including bulges, and check how your carrier rounds each dimension before multiplying — some round each side to the nearest whole inch first.</p>
  <h2>Reading the result</h2>
  <p>If dimensional weight is the larger number, reducing the box size lowers the billed weight even when the product weighs the same. The verdict line shows how much volume you would need to remove for dimensional weight to fall to the actual weight. Marketplace fulfillment programs use their own measurement and size-tier rules, which this calculator does not model; use the platform’s published tables for those fees.</p>
  <script>
    const $ = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id) as HTMLInputElement;
    function run() {
      const cm = $('u').value === 'cm'; const L = +$('l').value, W = +$('w').value, H = +$('h').value, A = +$('a').value, D = +$('d').value;
      const wu = cm ? 'kg' : 'lb', vu = cm ? 'cm³' : 'in³';
      const vol = L * W * H; $('o-vol').textContent = vol ? `${vol.toLocaleString('en-US', { maximumFractionDigits: 1 })} ${vu}` : '—';
      $('o-act').textContent = A ? `${A} ${wu}` : '—';
      if (!(D > 0) || !vol) { ['o-dim', 'o-bill', 'o-round'].forEach((i) => ($(i).textContent = '—')); $('o-v').textContent = 'Enter your carrier’s divisor to see the result.'; return; }
      const dim = vol / D, bill = Math.max(dim, A);
      $('o-dim').textContent = `${dim.toFixed(2)} ${wu}`; $('o-bill').textContent = `${bill.toFixed(2)} ${wu}`; $('o-round').textContent = `${Math.ceil(bill - 1e-9)} ${wu}`;
      $('o-v').textContent = dim > A ? `Dimensional weight is higher. Volume would need to fall by about ${(vol - A * D).toLocaleString('en-US', { maximumFractionDigits: 0 })} ${vu} (to ${(A * D).toLocaleString('en-US', { maximumFractionDigits: 0 })} ${vu}) for actual weight to govern.` : 'Actual weight is higher or equal, so the box size is not what drives the billed weight.';
    }
    document.getElementById('dw')!.addEventListener('input', run); run();
  </script>
</Tool>
